src/termio/stream_handler.zig:658:         // cursor blink with `cursor-style-blink`, the moment a running
src/termio/stream_handler.zig:659:         // program uses DEC mode 12, the cursor blink can never be reset
src/termio/stream_handler.zig:660:         // to the default without an explicit DECSCUSR. But if a program
src/termio/stream_handler.zig:661:         // is using mode 12, it is by definition not using DECSCUSR.
src/termio/stream_handler.zig:662:         // This makes for somewhat annoying interactions where a poorly
src/termio/stream_handler.zig:663:         // (or legacy) behaved program will stop blinking, and it simply
src/termio/stream_handler.zig:664:         // never restarts.
src/termio/stream_handler.zig:665:         //
